<BaseLayout title="Implementation, Onboarding & Enablement" current="/implementation-enablement/" description="Richard Allen's transferable experience in software migrations, onboarding, training, release validation, functional testing, product documentation, system transitions, and enablement.">
<section class="page-intro"><div class="container"><div class="eyebrow">Implementation, Onboarding & Enablement</div><h1>Help people adopt change with less friction.</h1><p class="lede">My experience is strongest where implementation connects customers, support teams, development, documentation, training, software validation, systems changes, and day-to-day adoption.</p></div></section>
<section class="section"><div class="container grid two">
  <article class="card"><h3>HawkSoft online migration</h3><p>Project-managed/coordinated customer database moves between local networks and HawkSoft Online and helped move hundreds of users from a prior online service to a substantially improved one, supporting customers through the technical, workflow, and training transition.</p></article>
  <article class="card"><h3>HawkSoft accounting-software redesign</h3><p>Led staff readiness for a major accounting-software change: communicated expectations six months in advance, arranged biweekly developer/staff education during the final two months, provided extra support and access to developers/management at go-live, and continued training for months afterward.</p></article>
  <article class="card"><h3>Bridge XLerator product documentation</h3><p>Surviving 2019 project material explicitly assigned me to document every Bridge XLerator feature and benefit for training, write user stories and business cases for features, document how each feature worked, and participate with the development team in product discussions and meetings.</p></article>
  <article class="card"><h3>Functional testing & defect documentation</h3><p>Performed systematic feature-by-feature testing of Bridge XLerator, reproduced defects, documented permission and test-coverage limitations, identified usability friction, and recommended interface and error-message improvements. I then connected release knowledge to procedure documentation, instructional videos, and customer education.</p></article>
  <article class="card"><h3>Shady Grove systems modernization</h3><p>Helped replace an older DOS-based X-ray film tracking system with a new system. Measurements taken as part of the transition showed an approximately 30% efficiency improvement. Also helped create the processes and procedures used to digitize thousands of X-ray films.</p></article>
  <article class="card"><h3>Willamette Broadband billing transition</h3><p>Was key in transitioning the company to a new billing system while handling customer service, billing, scheduling, troubleshooting, complaints, and customer training.</p></article>
  <article class="card"><h3>Training & enablement</h3><p>Trained customers and staff on software workflows, troubleshooting, features, product changes, and best practices; created training documentation, presentations, webinars, onboarding materials, SOPs, staff communications, and customer-facing instructional content.</p></article>
</div></section>
<section class="section tight"><div class="container"><p class="small"><strong>Scope note:</strong> This page describes documented implementation, onboarding, enablement, product-documentation, functional-testing, and software-release validation experience. It does not claim formal UAT ownership, formal product-roadmap ownership, or a dedicated Implementation Manager title.</p></div></section>
